# Coordinator

Import RoutesRead from "./routes_read.lg".
Import RoutesProblem from "./routes_problem.lg".
Import RoutesLease from "./routes_lease.lg".
Import Heartbeat from "./heartbeat.lg".
Import RoutesAttempt from "./routes_attempt.lg".
Import SmokeRun from "./smoke_run.lg".
Import CoordinatorDb from "./coordinator_db.lg".
Import DbLoad from "./db_load.lg".
Import LoadRules from "./load_rules.lg".
Import OpdpRun from "./opdp_run.lg".
Import OpdpPlan from "./opdp_plan.lg".

The factory's coordinator: the one process that holds the board. It serves the
worker API (`/api/v1/lease`, `/heartbeat`, `/attempt`), the read API the website
and auditors use, and the website itself, all from one route table over one
PostgreSQL database. Workers never touch the database; they see only these
routes, and every route checks what it is sent before anything is written.

The role is chosen by the factory's `roles.lg`: `factory coordinator` serves, and
`factory coordinator load <dir>` loads what an ingest role wrote, and `factory
coordinator smoke <base-url>` checks a running coordinator end to end.

One load: the problems first (a node names its problem), then the graph, then the
atlas profiles, then each problem's rank copied from its node, all on one
connection. A load that stops partway leaves what it loaded, and the next load of
the same directory completes it, because every statement is an idempotent upsert.

## Note
Serve the route table. `PORT` (or `LOGOS_PORT`) in the environment overrides the
port, and `LOGOS_HOST` the interface, as the standard server reads them.

## To serveCoordinator (port: Int):
    Serve on port port.

## Note
A coordinator command other than serving, from the program's arguments: the
program's name, `coordinator`, the command, then its arguments.

## To coordinatorCommand (xs: Seq of Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Let mutable a be ["", "", "", ""].
    Repeat for i from 3 to 6:
        If i is at most length of xs:
            Set item (i - 2) of a to item i of xs.
    If item 1 of a is equal to "load" and item 2 of a is not equal to "":
        Return loadIngested(item 2 of a).
    If item 1 of a is equal to "smoke" and item 2 of a is not equal to "":
        Return coordinatorSmoke(item 2 of a).
    If item 1 of a is equal to "plan":
        Return planOpenProblems().
    If item 1 of a is equal to "import-opdp" and item 4 of a is not equal to "":
        Return importOpdp(item 2 of a, item 3 of a, item 4 of a).
    Return a new Err with error "usage: factory coordinator [load <ingest-dir> | import-opdp <pin.json> <atlas.json.gz> <work-dir> | plan | smoke <base-url>]".

## Note
The atlas record files of a directory, in name order: `records.jsonl`, or the
`records-NNNN.jsonl` pieces an operator splits a large release into.

## To recordFiles (dir: Text) -> Seq of Text:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
    Inspect listDir(dir):
        When Ok (names):
            Repeat for name in names:
                If isRecordFile(name):
                    Push dir + "/" + name to out.
        When Err (e):
            Return out.
    Return out.

## Note
The directory `dir` loaded, or the first thing that stopped it.

## To loadIngested (dir: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Inspect dbOpen():
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (c):
            Let answer be loadOn(c, dir).
            Let closed be pgClose(c).
            Return answer.
    Return a new Err with error "no connection".

## To loadOn (c: PgConn, dir: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Inspect loadLines(c, dir + "/problems.jsonl", "problems", problemInsertSql()):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (problems):
            Inspect loadLines(c, dir + "/nodes.jsonl", "nodes", nodeInsertSql()):
                When Err (e):
                    Return a new Err with error e.
                When Ok (nodes):
                    Let mutable profiles be 0.
                    Repeat for path in recordFiles(dir):
                        Inspect loadLines(c, path, "records", profileUpdateSql()):
                            When Err (e):
                                Return a new Err with error e.
                            When Ok (n):
                                Set profiles to profiles + n.
                    Inspect pgQueryParams(c, rankSyncSql(), a new Seq of Text):
                        When Err (e):
                            Return a new Err with error e.
                        When Ok (qr):
                            Return a new Ok with value "loaded {problems} problems, {nodes} nodes and {profiles} atlas profiles from {dir}".
    Return a new Err with error "unloaded".
